------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Why this task started with questions instead of code
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Unlike items 5-9, item 10 had no "Required fix" checklist — it's a
before/after commercial-terms comparison, not a discrete bug. Reading the
actual code before touching anything showed the current subscription
system (publisher_subscriptions/business_subscriptions, PayFast
tokenized recurring billing, a full past_due -> grace_period -> suspended
lapse lifecycle built across three separate phases) was built entirely
around a MONTHLY model, while the new spec is a ONCE-OFF model. Several
things a developer would need decided before writing a line of code
weren't specified by the finding itself:
  - Does "once-off" mean no renewal ever, or a longer renewal period
    (e.g. annual)?
  - What happens to the R199 launch credit once there's no longer a
    "first of many" payment to tie it to?
  - "Secondary placements: from R99/month" isn't a concept that exists
    anywhere in the current code — what is it?
Getting any of these wrong would have meant rewriting real payment
integration code twice, so I asked before starting. Your answers:
  - Fully one-time, no renewal, ever.
  - Business fee becomes R399 (not R299 as the audit itself stated),
    with the R199 launch credit included in that fee rather than a
    separate purchase.
  - R99/month is the price for Featured/Advertise products, for both
    publishers and businesses, in-house (ChatSched's own inventory, not
    a third party).
Everything below implements exactly those three answers.

