3. Featured & Advertise, from R99/month
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Built the concrete, natural extension: self-serve recurring Featured
Placement for PUBLISHERS, reusing the exact PayFast recurring-billing
pattern this same task just retired from core membership (content-studio-
subscribe was the working template). This is the one genuinely recurring
product left after the once-off conversion above, so the pattern has a
real home again rather than sitting duplicated or discarded.

  - supabase/schema_phase87_featured_placement_subscriptions.sql (NEW) —
    a new table, keyed to a publisher's own listing (publishers.id, not
    profiles.id — this purchase targets a specific listing, unlike core
    membership). Deliberately simpler lifecycle than the old core-
    membership one: no grace period. A missed payment un-features the
    listing immediately (via a trigger, see below) rather than a
    forgiveness window — a reasonable, defensible policy for a cosmetic
    visibility boost rather than core marketplace access, and building a
    second full dunning system from scratch wasn't a proportionate use of
    this task's scope.
  - A trigger keeps publishers.featured/featured_until in sync with this
    table automatically. This was the key design decision that kept the
    change small: every existing "is this publisher featured" check
    (is_featured(), PublisherCard.tsx, Admin.tsx's own manual toggle)
    needed ZERO changes — the admin's existing manual-grant button and
    this new self-serve path both just write to the same two columns,
    independently, exactly as before.
  - supabase/functions/featured-placement-subscribe (NEW) — same shape as
    content-studio-subscribe, genuinely recurring PayFast fields kept.
  - supabase/functions/payfast-notify — new
    handleFeaturedPlacementSubscriptionItn branch, same pattern as the
    Content Studio branch it's modelled on.
  - src/components/FeaturedPlacementSection.tsx (NEW) + wired into
    src/pages/AccountSettings.tsx for publisher accounts — a real,
    working self-serve purchase button, not just a stated price with
    nowhere to act on it.

For BUSINESSES, the "Advertise" system (schema_phase51_advertise.sql)
covers five distinct products at genuinely different real-world price
points (banner ads, newsletter sponsorship, featured directory placement,
sponsored articles, brand partnerships) and was built inquiry-only by
deliberate design — its own header comment already said "no fixed rate
card yet." Converting all five to self-serve checkout is a materially
larger undertaking than this pricing-alignment task, so I delivered the
part that's actually a pricing fix: featured_placement now shows a real
starting price (R99/month, from the same shared constant) on the
Advertise page, rather than leaving that one product's price open-ended
forever. The inquiry flow itself is unchanged. This is a deliberate scope
boundary, not an oversight — see "what's not done" below.

